{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793705715965765001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"willing-evolvable-orca","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":2},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793699824936871001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"0effee60-56c9-49dc-afe5-78c905421151","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"d68f-4771-ebc1-4ee4"}],"description":"## Discovered from `d68f-4771-ebc1-4ee4`\n\n`d68f` made a `# mechanism-ok:` admission a two-way door: the marker's reason must open\nwith a SUNSET TICKET, and `check_no_open_sunset_marker` refuses to close that ticket while\nthe marker is still in the tree. Closing the sunset ticket is the project's statement that\nthe justification expired, so the close is blocked until the mechanism goes.\n\nThat rule is forward-only, and every admission already in the tree predates it.\n\n## The measured state\n\nMeasured against `origin/main` at `eba93991965`, harvesting with `d68f`'s own\n`sunset_ticket(marker_reason(line))` over the tree (excluding the grammar modules and the\nratchet's own fixtures):\n\n**24 marker sites name 19 distinct sunset tickets. All 19 are `closed`.**\n\n| Sunset ticket | Status | Marker sites |\n|---|---|---|\n| `dcc3-75ee-26ce-4840` | closed | `scripts/assert_volumes_in_service.py:2` |\n| `eebc-6aa1-e45b-4325` | closed | `scripts/check_terraform_tree_currency.py:2` |\n| `a68c-9633-248c-4b06` | closed | `scripts/check_user_data_size.py:2` |\n| `aa9e-3d35` | closed | `scripts/install_review_scanners.py:27`, `:28`, `:29`, `:30` |\n| `933f-e7d8-696a-4fbd` | closed | `src/rebar/_config_schema.py:235`, `src/rebar/_config_sections.py:92` |\n| `1cef-7fbc` | closed | `src/rebar/_config_schema.py:276` |\n| `48bd-1c15-c3b0-4a99` | closed | `src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:45` |\n| `2041-75d6-2a2f-4be9` | closed | `src/rebar/llm/config_readers.py:152`, `:157` |\n| `d279-4cf9` | closed | `src/rebar/llm/config_readers.py:257` |\n| `metaphoric-late-creature` (`7eaa-502b-3d0f-4b08`) | closed | `src/rebar/reconciler/_ref_lock.py:78` |\n| `4932-ea62-cf4f-451b` | closed | `src/rebar/similar/index.py:164` |\n| `b939-bc68-1cb2-4ee9` | closed | `tests/_child_hooks.py:1` |\n| `bab8-eb45-4dc2-4f02` | closed | `tests/_crash_guard.py:7` |\n| `7f3d-ddc9-04d9-4861` | closed | `tests/_observability_harness.py:1` |\n| `985f-0ec5-a61c-46ee` | closed | `tests/_sandbox_capabilities.py:3` |\n| `c6ce-4d8d-1c12-47cc` | closed | `tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_corroborator.py:23` |\n| `d730-8a25` | closed | `tests/unit/reconciler/test_acli_search_pagination.py:17` |\n| `aa9e-3d35-fd3e-41ee` | closed | `tests/unit/test_code_review_ws5.py:640` |\n| `68a9-2a6c-d9aa-49ad` | closed | `tests/unit/test_opcert_service_app.py:42` |\n\nSo the admission grammar's teeth bite on exactly zero of the admissions that exist. Every\none of the 24 is in the state `d68f` set out to forbid -- an admitted mechanism whose\nretirement ticket is already closed, with nothing left to retire it and no check that\nnotices. `d68f`'s close precheck cannot reach them, because it only fires at the moment a\nsunset ticket closes and these closed long before the grammar existed.\n\n## What is NOT the remedy\n\nAdding a lint-time check that fails when a marker's sunset ticket is closed would make the\nratchet read the store. `sunset_ticket`'s docstring (`src/rebar/_commands/sunset_markers.py:41-47`)\nstates why it does not: the lint-time ratchet runs in checkouts where the `tickets` ref\nneed not be fetched, so resolving an id there would add a dependency it does not have. A\nscan-time check is also a new `ci_gate` -- new mechanism installed to police mechanism,\nwhich is the inversion `6b48`'s tidying skill exists to stop. If a gate is wanted anyway,\nit is a separate idea for the operator, not part of this.\n\n## The remedy\n\nDischarge the backlog by hand, one site at a time. For each of the 24, exactly one of:\n\n- **remove the mechanism** -- the justification expired with its ticket, which is what the\n  closed sunset ticket asserts; this is the preferred outcome and shrinks the baseline\n- **repoint the marker** at a live ticket that will retire it, so the two-way door has\n  something to close against\n- **record that the mechanism is permanent** and so was never a sunset case, repointing it\n  at a ticket that says so\n\nThe third is a real category -- `src/rebar/reconciler/_ref_lock.py:78` admits\n`RefLockPushError`, which the marker itself notes is \"an error type, not a lock\", a\nmisdetection rather than an expiring justification. Those want a different disposition from\na genuinely expired admission, and conflating them is how the backlog formed.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Every marker site is dispositioned: removed, repointed at an open ticket, or\n      documented as a permanent non-sunset admission.\n- [ ] Re-running the harvest over the tree reports zero marker sites whose sunset ticket is\n      `closed`.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` passes, with any resulting shrink\n      drained via `--update-stale` in the same change.\n- [ ] No new `ci_gate`, `env_var`, `config_key` or other mechanism is added by this work.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes.\n\n## Provider neutrality\n\nNo model, vendor or harness is involved; this is tree surgery and tracker reads.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"cbf7-3502-10d8-4c84","ticket_type":"story","title":"Discharge the 24 mechanism-ok admissions whose sunset tickets are already closed","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["57017752-aaf1-4338-a077-6037e0f12cde","0effee60-56c9-49dc-afe5-78c905421151"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793705715965765001,"uuid":"e72978c2-e18a-49d3-b0b4-f83de797c3dd"}